 ("p", "This is called the **'by' exception**: surprise, pleasure, interest, concern verbs take at / with / in / to instead of by. E.g., *The news surprised me.* - *I was surprised at the news.* *The sight pleased her.* - *She was pleased with the sight.* *Music interests him.* - *He is interested in music.* *The result disappointed us.* - *We were disappointed with the result.* *His name is known to everyone.*"),
